  "readmeFile": "README.md",
  "releaseNotes": "Strong name: Microsoft.Exchange.WebServices.dll and Sunsetless.Ews.Core.dll are signed with the Sunsetless key (public key token 1b8c25c6fc94dcf1), so strong-named .NET Framework applications and components can reference them. This changes the assembly identity: on .NET Framework, rebuild every project that references the library against this version, because assemblies compiled against 1.2.1 or earlier do not load the signed DLL. On .NET 8, 9 and 10 the strong name changes nothing. WellKnownFolderName has the numeric values of Microsoft's package: from ArchiveRoot on they used to differ, so a library compiled against Microsoft's package, or a folder stored as a number, could open another folder. Rebuild code compiled against 1.x that uses these folders. When Microsoft's Microsoft.Exchange.WebServices package is also in a build, this package's Microsoft.Exchange.WebServices.dll wins (file version 15.x) and the build warns with SUNSETLESS001. Components that ship the library can supply their own license key with SunsetlessEws.UseComponentLicense. Projects that target .NET Framework 3.5, 4.0 and 4.5 can reference the package: routing to Microsoft Graph then needs .NET Framework 4.7.2 or newer on the computer, and a .NET Framework 3.5 application must run on the .NET Framework 4 runtime (supportedRuntime v4.0 in its .config file); requests to Exchange Server work without either. FindItem cuts long extended property values (PR_BODY, PR_HTML and others) to 255 characters or 510 bytes in every query path, as Exchange Online does, and BodyType.HTML returns a plain-text message as HTML. GetConversationItems returns the extended properties of a message as Exchange Online does: only those in its conversation view, with strings cut to 255 characters, while meeting messages, posts and messages with voting come back in full. GetConversationItems orders nodes as Exchange Online does: newest first when no SortOrder is sent (the EWS Managed API overload that takes a list of conversations never sends one), replies newest first in TreeOrderAscending, and MaxItemsToReturn keeps the newest items. SUNSETLESS_BRIDGE_ALL_HOSTS=true (BridgeAllHosts in the options) sends calls to every host to Microsoft Graph, Exchange Server included, for applications that still call an Exchange Server URL after their mailboxes moved to Exchange Online. Supported operations, verification against live Exchange Online and known differences: https://sunsetless.com/compatibility",
